93	    /**
94	     Get the data that this form submits. The returned list is computed fresh on each call, in the document order of
95	     the controls associated with this form, and is independent of the DOM (which is not modified). Multiple controls
96	     sharing the same name are each included as separate {@link Connection.KeyVal}s.
97	     <p>Controls are skipped when they are themselves disabled, or are inside a disabled {@code fieldset} &mdash;
98	     except for controls within the subtree of that fieldset's first {@code legend}. A nested disabled fieldset is not
99	     exempted by an outer fieldset's legend.</p>
100	     <p>For {@code select} controls: a single select submits the first enabled selected option, or, if none is marked
101	     selected, the first enabled option; a {@code multiple} select submits all enabled selected options, in order.
102	     Disabled options, and options within a disabled {@code optgroup}, are not eligible. A select with no eligible
103	     option contributes no data.</p>
104	     <p>Checkboxes and radio inputs contribute only when checked. {@code input} controls of type {@code button} and
105	     {@code image}, and all {@code button} elements, are not submitted; other types (including {@code submit} and
106	     {@code reset}) are included as before.</p>
107	     @return a new, independent list of key vals
108	     */
109	    public List<Connection.KeyVal> formData() {
110	        ArrayList<Connection.KeyVal> data = new ArrayList<>();
111	
112	        // iterate the form control elements in document order and accumulate their values
113	        Elements formEls = elements();
114	        for (Element el: formEls) {
115	            if (!el.tag().isFormSubmittable()) continue; // contents are form listable, superset of submitable
116	            if (el.nameIs("button")) continue; // button elements are never submitted by formData()
117	            if (el.hasAttr("disabled")) continue; // skip disabled form inputs
118	            if (inDisabledFieldset(el)) continue; // skip controls held in a disabled fieldset (outside its first legend)
119	            String name = el.attr("name");
120	            if (name.length() == 0) continue;
121	            String type = el.attr("type");
122	
